loopcatcher (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Replace the hand-rolled ANSI TUI with charmbracelet/gum widgets (fixed
    width 100, rounded borders, terminal-default colours, margin/padding).
  * Add player profiles. "spotify" fills the detection fields; "custom" lets
    the user edit sink_app_name / player_mpris_bus / player_sink_match by hand.
    All four are persisted to the config file. The MPRIS D-Bus monitor is
    scoped to the selected player so other media players no longer trigger a
    recording.
  * Onboarding is now a one-time gum wizard, shown only when the config file is
    absent (player profile, codec, bitrate, filename scheme, output directory);
    it ends with a single "Continue" choice and saves by default.
  * The session name prompt suggests a timestamped name ("<date>-<time>-
    loopcatcher"); just press Enter. Session setup is entered directly.
  * New guided "no sink" wizard replaces the blocking notice: it polls for the
    player sink, walks the play/pause setup, then confirms.
  * Session ends automatically ("Recording finished, exiting...") instead of
    waiting for a keypress.
  * Replace the q/c/r/a/l key commands with a gum choose menu (any key opens
    Resume / Config / Reload config / About / License / Quit).
  * Config menu is grouped: Codecs, Paths, Player, Advanced.
  * Every screen shows the title panel. Status view: title, a metadata gum
    table, and a bottom row split into an instructions box and a live-status
    box (bold State:/Playback: labels) joined horizontally. The screen is
    cleared before every gum prompt so nothing stacks.
  * player_profile_label prints "Custom Player" for the custom profile.
  * Bold title text and "Press any key to open the menu" (CLICOLOR_FORCE keeps
    gum styling through the nested status_render composition). Clear the
    terminal on exit.
  * Status view: no more spinner (it caused constant flicker while recording);
    the view is redrawn only on real changes. Dropped the left/right split -
    now three stacked boxes below the title: session info (Session Name /
    Audio Sink / Config File / Output Folder), the metadata table (Artist /
    Album / Track / Output File, path relative to the session folder), and the
    status box (Catcher Status / Playback Status + the menu hint).
  * The no-sink flow is now a three-step "Recording Wizard" with a shared title
    bar and a bold, centred "Step N" heading over left-aligned instructions:
    Step 1 "Create the Audio Sink", Step 2 "Prepare to record" (waits for the
    pause; no more "Ready?" confirm prompt), Step 3 "Start recording" (the
    pre-first-play status screen). q cancels and exits on every step.
  * Session name prompt: the suggested timestamp name is now the placeholder, so
    pressing Enter on an empty field accepts it; a rejected entry is kept in the
    field for editing instead of being lost. Reject "." and ".." (and, as before,
    names containing "/") in both the prompt and --session.
  * Hardening pass: atomic config writes (mktemp + mv), exact-match null-sink
    detection (an awk token match, no more substring greps), mkdir failure is
    fatal with a clear message, "mkdir -p --" everywhere, the main loop snapshots
    the dbus coproc fd so "set -u" cannot abort when the monitor exits, and the
    dependency check lists the text tools it actually uses.
  * Kill the remaining status-view flicker: each screen is now composed in full
    (all gum calls) before a single write to the terminal - no clear-then-wait
    gap. The live view repaints at most once per loop tick and only when
    something changed, skips the write when the frame is byte-identical, and
    reuses a precomputed title + session-info box (about 3 gum calls per repaint,
    down from ~13). The menu draws on the status view's own alternate screen
    instead of swapping screens twice.
  * On session end, a tooltip screen announces the finish and the session path
    and waits for a keypress before exiting (was an immediate exit).
  * Open the menu with the "m" key (was any key); the menu is a gum filter
    (type to narrow). Config-menu items use human-readable labels and no
    longer show the config file path.
  * Code review / cleanup: single `ui_screen` helper for every gum screen
    (clear + bold title + gap); onboarding steps each get their own screen;
    editing a Player detection field in the config menu now flips the profile
    to "custom" so the change is not reverted on reload; suppress WINCH while a
    menu/pager is open so a resize can't paint the status view over it; fold
    the gum dependency check into check_dependencies with an install hint.
  * The session-name prompt can be cancelled with Esc (exits cleanly).
  * Add gum to Depends.

 -- Kike Fonseca <filipok@gmail.com>  Sat, 29 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000

loopcatcher (0.1.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release as loopcatcher.
  * Generic loopback audio capture positioning and documentation.
  * Keep sink default name as "spotify" for compatibility.
  * Interactive TUI with runtime config menu and session output handling.
  * Debian packaging metadata and desktop integration.
  * Relicense the project under the MIT (Expat) License.

